                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7679019" data-guid="7679019"></div>
        <div id="questions-7679019" data-guid="7679019" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7679019_content" title-footnotes="1"><div class="history">[Added<span class="legref" data-ref="LF1684293"><span class="hisdate">11-7-2022</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 7-2022 (F-2022)</span></span>]</div><div class="para">There is hereby established a department known as the “Department of Public Safety.”</div><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7679019-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7679019-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor’s Note: Former § 42-69, Establishment, was repealed 12-2-2013 by L.L. No. 5-2013.</div></div></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h3"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7679020 child"
      id="7679020"
      data-guid="7679020"
      data-parent-guid="7679018"
      data-position="1005"
      data-full-title="§ 42-70: Commissioner of Public Safety."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7679020_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7679020_label" for="7679020_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7679020"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 42-70
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7679020"
    >
Commissioner of Public Safety.    </span>
    </a>
    <span class="titleFootnotes">
        <a id="ref7679020-1"
           href="#ft7679020-1"
           class="footnoteref"
        >
          [1]
        </a>
    </span>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7679020" data-guid="7679020"></div>
        <div id="questions-7679020" data-guid="7679020" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7679020_content" title-footnotes="1"><div class="history">[Added<span class="legref" data-ref="LF1684293"><span class="hisdate">11-7-2022</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 7-2022 (F-2022)</span></span>]</div><div class="para">There shall be appointed by the Mayor a Commissioner of Public Safety who shall head the Department of Public Safety and carry out the functions and duties thereof. The Commissioner shall serve and hold such office at the pleasure of the Mayor. The Commissioner shall appoints such deputies, directors and other subordinates as shall be authorized by the Board of Estimate and Apportionment and who shall serve at the Commissioner's pleasure.</div><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7679020-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7679020-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor’s Note: Former § 42-70, Commissioner of Public Safety, was repealed 12-2-2013 by L.L. No. 5-2013.</div></div></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h3"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7679021 child"
      id="7679021"
      data-guid="7679021"
      data-parent-guid="7679018"
      data-position="1006"
      data-full-title="§ 42-71: Scope, powers, and duties of Commissioner."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7679021_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7679021_label" for="7679021_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7679021"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 42-71
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7679021"
    >
Scope, powers, and duties of Commissioner.    </span>
    </a>
    <span class="titleFootnotes">
        <a id="ref7679021-1"
           href="#ft7679021-1"
           class="footnoteref"
        >
          [1]
        </a>
    </span>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-7679021" data-guid="7679021"></div>
        <div id="questions-7679021" data-guid="7679021" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="7679021_content" title-footnotes="1"><div class="history">[Added <span class="legref" data-ref="LF1684293"><span class="hisdate">11-7-2022</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 7-2022 (F-2022)</span></span>; amended <span class="legref" data-ref="LF1849060"><span class="hisdate">6-5-2023</span> by <span class="loclaw">L.L. No. 8-2023 (Q-2022)</span></span>]</div><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="42479464"><a alt="42-71A" class="litem_number" href="42479464#42479464" onclick="return false;" title="42-71A">A. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The Commissioner of Public Safety shall serve as the designated arbiter of any disciplinary determination that is appealed from within the Albany Police Department. The Commissioner shall have the authority to hold hearings, and issue final binding discipline in such matters. In addition, the Commissioner shall possess such other powers and perform such other duties as may be prescribed by local law or ordinance of the Common Council.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="42479465"><a alt="42-71B" class="litem_number" href="42479465#42479465" onclick="return false;" title="42-71B">B. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">If the Commissioner produces a written determination on matters in which there is a corresponding Community Police Review Board (CPRB) investigation, they shall provide a copy of such written determination to the Chief of Police, any individual who is the subject of the disciplinary proceeding, and the CPRB.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="42479466"><a alt="42-71C" class="litem_number" href="42479466#42479466" onclick="return false;" title="42-71C">C. </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">On any matter which is before the Commissioner, the Commissioner shall be provided with any and all CPRB recommendations and findings which were provided to the Chief of Police in such matter. The Commissioner shall review and consider the CPRB's recommendations and findings, if any, and, if they disagree with any such recommendations and/or findings, they shall state the basis for such disagreement in any written determination they produce related to the matter.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7679021-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7679021-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor’s Note: Former § 42-71, Scope, powers, and duties of Commissioner, was repealed 12-2-2013 by L.L. No. 5-2013.</div></div></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h3"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 7679022 child"
      id="7679022"
      data-guid="7679022"
      data-parent-guid="7679018"
      data-position="1010"
      data-full-title="§ 42-72: Police Department reporting requirements."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="7679022_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="7679022_label" for="7679022_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#7679022"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      § 42-72
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="7679022"
